            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0878" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24 Raw Materials/3002: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-07">September 7,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>827. Your 1486, September 6, 8 p.m., paragraph 2. The American Minister at The
                    Hague has been requested to press the Netherland Government for agreement to the
                    proposed special 10 percent release for the fourth quarter and to keep you
                    informed directly. Please keep The Hague informed regarding developments in
                    London affecting rubber.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
